WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.996
In this video, you will review the homes your neighbors enter.

00:00:03.996 --> 00:00:09.648
You will approve the good ones, decline the ones that do not fit, and learn how to undo a mistake.

00:00:09.648 --> 00:00:10.789
We start on the map.

00:00:11.691 --> 00:00:13.440
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.404 --> 00:00:17.921
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:20.645
Then tap Allow.

00:00:24.654 --> 00:00:27.344
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.344 --> 00:00:28.539
See the three dots?

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:32.842
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:32.842 --> 00:00:33.380
Tap them.

00:00:34.983 --> 00:00:36.796
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:43.577
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.194
Tap Mine.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.666
This is your personal page.

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:53.851
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.623
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:58.444 --> 00:01:01.857
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:03.730
Now tap Entries.

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.910
This is where you review every home that neighbors enter.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:14.847
Nothing goes on the map until you approve it, which protects your contest from photos that do not belong.

00:01:15.755 --> 00:01:19.028
Each entry shows the photos, the address, and who sent it.

00:01:19.028 --> 00:01:20.747
If it looks right, tap Approve.

00:01:22.502 --> 00:01:27.622
The home joins the contest, appears on the map, and shows up on every voter's ballot.

00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:30.182
The neighbor is emailed to say they are in.

00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:37.422
If an entry does not belong, for example, the photo is not a home, or it is a duplicate, tap Decline.

00:01:39.155 --> 00:01:40.771
A small window asks why.

00:01:40.771 --> 00:01:46.591
The reason is optional, but a kind note helps the neighbor fix the problem and try again.

00:01:46.591 --> 00:01:48.078
It is emailed to them.

00:01:48.078 --> 00:01:49.565
Then tap Decline entry.

00:01:51.448 --> 00:01:52.604
Changed your mind?

00:01:52.604 --> 00:01:54.429
A declined entry is not gone.

00:01:54.429 --> 00:01:59.234
Tap Restore and it goes back to waiting for your review, so you can approve it.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.884
Next up: Edit your contest and change the dates.
